function actually lives. This was what kept `tests/test_search.py` from loading.\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` kept the year as text (`\"1965\"`), which also broke `age()`. It now converts the year to a number.\n- **`factory.py`**: the sample data was missing `Emma`, which the docstring says should be there. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The author, year and copies are my choice; the tests only check the title.\n- **`fees.py`**: the fee was `days_late + DAILY_FEE` instead of `days_late * DAILY_FEE`, so one day late cost 1.25 instead of 0.25.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`. I also made it return an empty list when `n` is 0 or less, because the slice `[-0:]` would otherwise return the whole history.\n- **`members.py`**: the borrowing limit was 3, but the comment above it and the tests both say 5. Changed it to 5.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "run_id": "opencode:make-ci-green:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "sampling_observed": null, "score": 1.0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 17.42, "t_checker_s": 0.228, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "make-ci-green", "timeout_s": 840, "token_basis": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1201, "tokens_cache_read": 32375, "tokens_cache_write": 43373, "tokens_fresh": 1201, "tokens_input_uncached": 10, "tokens_output": 1191, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 32375, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 43373, "tokens_proxy_calls": 4, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 10, "tokens_proxy_output": 1191, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "6.0.168", "anthropic": "3.0.64", "bun": "1.3.13"}, "trial": 2, "ts_iso": "2026-10-05T16:43:58", "turns": 4, "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15164}, "input": 4, "output": 101, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15269}, {"cache": {"read": 15164, "write": 2047}, "input": 2, "output": 124, "reasoning": 0, "total": 17337}, {"cache": {"read": 